/* Windows resource script — gives openyog.exe its own icon in Explorer, the
 * taskbar and Alt-Tab. QApplication::setWindowIcon() (qt/main.cpp) only dresses
 * the window at runtime; the file itself needs a real ICON resource, or the
 * shell falls back to the generic executable glyph.
 *
 * Resource id 1 (numeric, not a named identifier): the shell shows the
 * lowest-numbered icon resource as the file's icon, so this is unambiguous
 * regardless of anything else linked in later. Compiled by windres only on
 * Windows builds — see the WIN32 block in CMakeLists.txt, which also puts
 * qt/ on the resource-compiler include path so the path below resolves.
 */
1 ICON "resources/openyog.ico"
